{"folioDeck": 1, "exportedAt": 1793318400000, "meta": {"id": "jakata", "title": "Japanese — Katakana", "subtitle": "The 121 katakana, for loanwords — study after hiragana", "desc": "The second syllabary, learnt after hiragana: katakana, used for words borrowed from other languages (コーヒー, テレビ), foreign names, and emphasis. 121 notes, each with TWO cards (katakana → romaji, romaji → katakana): the same 104 sounds as the hiragana deck, the long-vowel mark ー, and the 15 combinations used only to spell loanwords (ファ, ティ, ウィ…). The romaji is Hepburn. Each card shows the matching hiragana and, where the JLPT decks have one, a loanword that begins with the kana, with its reading and meaning. Study before JLPT N5, after hiragana. — Example words: Jonathan Waller's JLPT lists (CC BY) and JMdict (EDRDG, CC BY-SA 4.0).", "author": "", "language": "en", "color": "#BC002D", "tags": ["japanese", "katakana", "kana", "writing"], "glossMode": "site", "types": {"kana": {"id": "kana", "name": "Japanese kana", "speechLang": "ja-JP", "fields": ["Kana", "Romaji", "Note", "Pair", "Examples"], "cards": [{"name": "Katakana → romaji", "front": "<div class=\"uc-kana\">{{Kana}}</div>", "back": "{{FrontSide}}<hr><div class=\"uc-romaji\">{{Romaji}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Kana}}\"></span></div>{{#Note}}<div class=\"uc-note\">{{Note}}</div>{{/Note}}{{#Pair}}<div class=\"uc-pair\">{{Pair}}</div>{{/Pair}}{{#Examples}}<div class=\"uc-eg\">{{Examples}}</div>{{/Examples}}"}, {"name": "Romaji → katakana", "front": "<div class=\"uc-ask\">Write it in katakana</div><div class=\"uc-romaji\">{{Romaji}}</div>{{#Note}}<div class=\"uc-note\">{{Note}}</div>{{/Note}}", "back": "{{FrontSide}}<hr><div class=\"uc-kana\">{{Kana}}<span class=\"uc-tts uc-say\" data-say=\"{{Kana}}\"></span></div>{{#Pair}}<div class=\"uc-pair\">{{Pair}}</div>{{/Pair}}{{#Examples}}<div class=\"uc-eg\">{{Examples}}</div>{{/Examples}}"}], "css": ".card { text-align: center; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; }\n.uc-ask { m